        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive mirror of the patterns already established in this codebase:\n\n- **Service layer** \u2014 `assertDailyCapacity` / `countOwnersRegisteredOn` are structurally parallel to the existing `assertCityCapacity` / `countOwnersInCity` (same guard-clause + count-and-throw shape, same `ownerRepository.findAll().stream()...count()` idiom). The `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT` constant is placed directly above its method, exactly as `CITY_OWNER_LIMIT` is. The call site is added inside the existing `owner.isNew()` block alongside the sibling capacity check, which is the right unit for this \"on create\" validation.\n- **Exception** \u2014 `DailyOwnerLimitException` lives in the same package as `CityOwnerLimitException`, extends `RuntimeException`, and builds its message in the constructor the same way.\n- **Advice** \u2014 `handleDailyOwnerLimitException` is a line-for-line analog of `handleCityOwnerLimitException`, differing only in the exception type and the intended status (429 vs 409), consistent with the spec.\n\nNothing is duplicated in a way that begs extraction (the count helpers legitimately filter on different fields), no class is becoming a catch-all, and a maintainer of this codebase would find each piece exactly where the existing capacity/limit feature taught them to look."
